Drill 9 — New-to-Dataset, Recurring, Reactivated, and Dormant Revenue Engine
Exact task statement
Classify customer activity each month into new-to-dataset, recurring, reactivated, and dormant states.
Build order
33.	Create a customer-month activity table.
34.	Find first_seen_month and prior_active_month for each customer-month.
35.	Assign customer_status for each active month.
36.	Summarize revenue by status and count dormant customers separately.
Validation checks
•	Status buckets for active months must be mutually exclusive.
•	New plus recurring plus reactivated revenue must equal active revenue for the month.
•	Dormant customers should not appear in active buckets for that same month.
Final output template
revenue_month	active_customer_count	new_to_dataset_revenue	recurring_revenue	reactivated_revenue	dormant_customer_count
2025-11-01	5118	8400000	129700000	5800000	216
Output column definitions
•	new_to_dataset_revenue = revenue from customers whose current month equals first_seen_month.
•	recurring_revenue = revenue from customers active in both current month and immediately prior month.
•	reactivated_revenue = revenue from customers active now, inactive last month, but active earlier.

--===========================================================================================================
With cte_1 as
(Select
	customer_code,
	oracle_customer_name,
	rev_mth_dt,
	Sum(amount) customer_revenue	
From platinum.txn_normalized
Group by
	customer_code,
	oracle_customer_name,
	rev_mth_dt
),
cte_2 as(
Select
	*,
	Min(rev_mth_dt) over(partition by customer_code) as first_seen_month,
	date_trunc('Month', rev_mth_dt -1)::date as immediate_prior_month
From cte_1
),
cte_3 as
(
Select 
	customer_code,
	oracle_customer_name,
	rev_mth_dt,
	immediate_prior_month,
	first_seen_month,	
	customer_revenue as current_revenue,
	Case
		when rev_mth_dt = first_seen_month Then customer_revenue
		Else 0
	End as new_to_dataset_revenue,
	Case
		When 
			(Lag(rev_mth_dt) over(partition by customer_code order by rev_mth_dt))::date = date_trunc('Month', rev_mth_dt - 1)::date 
		Then 
			customer_revenue
		Else 0
	End as recurring_revenue,
	Case
		When 
			(Lag(rev_mth_dt) over(partition by customer_code order by rev_mth_dt))::date <> date_trunc('Month', rev_mth_dt - 1)::date 
			And rev_mth_dt <> first_seen_month
		Then 
			customer_revenue
		Else 0
	End as reactivate_revenue
From cte_2
)
Select
	rev_mth_dt,
	Count(*) as active_customer_count,
	Sum(current_revenue) as current_revenue,
	Sum(new_to_dataset_revenue) as new_to_dataset_revenue,
	Sum(recurring_revenue) as recurring_revenue,
	Sum(reactivate_revenue) as reactivate_revenue,
From cte_3
Group by
	rev_mth_dt







	


